    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented for **version 2 of the owner identity**.\n\n## Response shape\n- **`openapi.yml`**: Added a new `Identity` schema (memberId, householdId, identityKey), removed those three from the top\u2011level `Owner`, and added `identity` (grouping them) plus a top\u2011level integer `apiVersion` example `2`.\n- **`OwnerMapper`**: Removed the flat `identityKey` mapping, added `apiVersion` (constant `2`) and `identity` mappings, and a new `identity(owner)` method that builds the `IdentityDto`.\n\n## Version\u20112 region seam (mixes in a fixed `V2` tag)\n- **`MemberIds.identifierRegion`** now returns `plainRegionOf(owner) + \"V2\"` \u2014 the single seam every identifier reads its region through. `plainRegionOf` (used by `locality`, `timezone`, `ownerSegment`) is untouched, so the V2 tag never leaks into user\u2011facing fields.\n- **`Households.id`** now hashes `identifierRegion | lastName | postcode`.\n- **`OwnerIdentity.key`** now hashes `identifierRegion | telephone | email | soundex(lastName)`.\n\nBecause the region seam feeds all three, every identifier (`memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`) changes and no v1 value recurs; duplicate detection stays consistent since existing owners recompute their keys the same way.\n\n## Audit schema v2\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** gained `schemaVersion` (=2) and `ownerSegment`, recomputed via a new shared **`OwnerSegments`** helper (also used by the mapper). The event now serializes `{schemaVersion, seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment, event}`.\n\n## Verification\nObserved at runtime: `memberId=NSWV22716E6609E7`, audit `{\"schemaVersion\":2,...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",...}`, and the response has `apiVersion=2` with the nested `identity` object. `ownerSegment` stays `STANDARD_METRO` (plain region \u2192 METRO), confirming the V2 tag is confined to identifiers.\n\nFull test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec's \"recompute the owner segment from the version-2 identity\" was ambiguous since the segment's region must stay plain \u2014 I added `ownerSegment` to the audit event computed from the plain region + capped level (matching the response field), which is the only reading consistent with \"the V2 tag never appears in the owner segment's derived region.\" No test pins the audit event contents, so this is the faithful-but-uncorroborated part.",
