    "probe_text": "I now have the full pipeline. Here is every validation and side-effect applied by `POST /api/owners`, in execution order.\n\n## Pre-pipeline\n\n1. **Authorization** (`owners.POST.yml` `composition.authorize`): caller must satisfy `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, else `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403). Applies before any step runs.\n\nThe whole pipeline runs under a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), committed once at the end.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `CheckIdempotency`\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and **publishes it** as a variable (`Out<String>`) for later recording.\n- If the key was already seen: loads the originally-created owner and throws `IdempotentReplayException`, short-circuiting to a **200 replay** (no new owner created). This deliberately runs *before* the duplicate check so a repeat gives 200, not 409.\n- Note: this runs *before* body validation \u2014 a replayed request never validates its body.\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `BuildOwner` (binds `@RequestBody @Valid`, the only body-reading step)\nApplied in this internal order:\n- **Bean validation** on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`, runs before the method body): `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotNull`, name `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`; `city` `@NotNull @Size(1..80)`; `telephone` `@NotNull @Size(1..20)`; `address` `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` `@Size(max 255)`; `email` `@Email @Size(max 255)`; `postcode` `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`; `title` enum. Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (400).\n- **Side-effect:** publishes the request-only `sharesHousehold` flag as a variable.\n- **Side-effect:** normalizes address fields \u2014 `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE), then composes the effective `address` (structured lines preferred over flat).\n- **Validation:** required-field check on the *composed* result \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` if any missing.\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (assumes `+61`, drops leading `0`, strips separators; enforces 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalizes optional `email` to lower-case; syntactic check and disposable-domain rejection (`mailinator.com`/`tempmail.com`/`guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException`.\n- **Validation:** optional `postcode` must fall in the city's region range (NSW/VIC/QLD); unknown region accepts any 4-digit \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- **Side-effect:** maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity.\n- **Validation:** supplied `registrationDate` may not be in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`; if absent, defaults to today.\n- **Side-effect:** rolls `registrationDate` forward to the next non-holiday business day and stores it. Publishes the built `Owner`.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `AssignHousehold`\n- **Side-effect:** sets deterministic `householdId` = SHA-256(lastName + postcode) (first 12 hex). Unconditional; used only for household-size/membership derivations now, not duplicate detection.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (the hard duplicate check)\n- **Validation:** unless `sharesHousehold` is true, rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (409) if any existing non-soft-deleted owner has the same `identityKey` = SHA-256(identifierRegion + normalized telephone + lower email + soundex(lastName)). Declared household members bypass this.\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `AssignMemberId`\n- **Side-effect:** computes `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`); on collision with an existing `memberId`, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique. Sets it on the owner.\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount`\n- **Side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `EnsureCityCapacity`\n- **Validation:** rejects with `CityAtCapacityException` if the owner's city (normalized, case-insensitive) already has \u2265 50 owners.\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`\n- **Validation:** rejects with `DailyOwnerLimitException` if \u2265 100 existing owners share this owner's (adjusted) `registrationDate`.\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (soft match)\n- **Side-effect:** unless `sharesHousehold` is true, flags `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <earliest matching id>` when an existing non-deleted owner has a *different* identityKey but the *same* soundex(lastName) and postcode; otherwise sets `possibleDuplicate = false`.\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n- **Side-effect:** persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the DB id).\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `RecordIdempotency`\n- **Side-effect:** if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore` so a repeat replays this owner. No-op when no key.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** computes membership points and capped level; emits a human-readable audit line **and** a structured schema-v2 `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON (allocating a monotonic app-wide `seq`) to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`\n- **Side-effect:** emits a welcome line (`id`, `memberId`) to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n- **Side-effect:** maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth flagging while reading it as-is:\n- The idempotency replay in step 1 happens **before** body validation (step 2), so a replayed key returns the stored owner without re-validating the (possibly different) body.\n- The `sharesHousehold` DTO doc says it bypasses duplicates for \"same last name and postcode,\" but the actual hard check it bypasses (`EnsureUniqueIdentity`) keys on telephone + email + soundex(lastName), not last name + postcode \u2014 the last-name/postcode notion now only drives the *soft* match in step 9."
